# UI design reuse (TaskOS)

When adding or changing frontend UI in this project:

1. **Reuse first** — look for an existing component/pattern before inventing a new one.
2. **Date picking** — use `JalaliDateField` / `JalaliMonthCalendar` (same as dashboard day picker / PastDaysMenu). Do **not** use `input type="datetime-local"` or browser-native scroll time wheels.
3. **Time picking** — use styled `<select>` (or the same control language as existing forms), not scroll spinners.
4. **Modals** — follow `AgingModal` / `TaskReminderModal`: `fixed inset-0`, `bg-black/70 backdrop-blur`, rounded-2xl/`#141824` panel, RTL.
5. **Colors** — stick to established accents: amber (priority/focus), sky (comments), teal (khadang), violet (reminders), rose (danger). Do not introduce loud one-off themes.
6. **Nav / mobile** — hamburger is an overlay drawer (`fixed` + scrim); desktop keeps the top nav strip.
7. **Lists** — long lists (notifications, reminders, “all …” tabs) need client pagination (~15–20 per page).

If a new surface cannot reuse an existing piece, extend that piece instead of forking a parallel design.
